From 600cdef7c92ea59a5578c49f83def0fb9168698f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brian Woods
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 19:14:59 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] perf(quant): launch one grouped dynamic LoRA kernel per site

The CUDA dynamic LoRA path launched a shrink and an expand kernel for every active
adapter at every site. With several adapters in a batch that is many small launches
per decode step. Add grouped kernels that handle all adapters in one launch pair: each
block looks up its row's adapter in a per-execution row table, and the adapters' weight
pointers, ranks and scales travel by value (up to 32 per launch, chunked beyond that).
The arithmetic is unchanged, so output matches the per-adapter path bit for bit. A single
active adapter keeps the existing path.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
